<title>USA: Colorado defeats measure on tax-exempt status.</title>
<headline>Colorado defeats measure on tax-exempt status.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A controversial ballot initiative in Colorado to take away the tax exempt status of churches and charitable organizations appeared headed for defeat, according to local media reports.</p>
<p>With 40 percent of the vote in, the so-called Amendment 11 was trailing 83 percent to 17 percent.</p>
<p>Churches and other groups campaigned heavily against the measure.</p>
</text>
